; TEST: abort=1 c-emit-exit=4
;
; `div u8 5 0`: a zero divisor traps at every width and both signs (spec
; 5.4, "trapping `+ - * /`, zero divisor" -- prelude/README.md's abort kind
; 1, the shared `bfausr_trap`). The check is the first two lines of the
; emitted sequence, before anything is divided:
;
;       mov     rcx, [rbp-24]
;       test    rcx, rcx
;       jz      bfausr_trap
;
; and it is a RUNTIME check even here, where the divisor is a constant 0:
; nothing in this backend folds, and whether a constant-folded trapping op
; should instead be a compile-time diagnostic is still `[OPEN]` (ssa-ir.md
; 6 -- it would need a spec 13 code, and none is proposed).
;
; Without it the hardware would raise #DE: SIGFPE, exit 136, not this
; tree's numeric trap. So the mutation is loud in the right way.
;
; Mutation (run): the `test`/`jz` pair dropped -> exit 136 (SIGFPE) instead
; of 132 (SIGILL), i.e. abort kind detection fails rather than the exit
; status silently matching.
;
; If nothing traps the function returns 7.
;
; `c-emit-exit=4`: the C backend refuses `div` by name (c-backend.md D4 row
; 4), so the differential phase checks parity of that refusal.

functio @initium (ptr) -> u8 {
b0:
%0 = param ptr 0
%1 = iconst u8 5
%2 = iconst u8 0
%3 = div u8 %1 %2
%4 = iconst u8 7
ret %4
}
